#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-opt-report.md:1
msgid "llvm-opt-report - generate optimization report from YAML"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-opt-report.md:6
msgid "SYNOPSIS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-opt-report.md:8
msgid "{program}`llvm-opt-report` \\[*options*\\] [input]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-opt-report.md:10
msgid "DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-opt-report.md:12
msgid ""
"{program}`llvm-opt-report` is a tool to generate an optimization report from "
"YAML optimization record files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-opt-report.md:14
msgid ""
"You need to create an input YAML optimization record file before running "
"{program}`llvm-opt-report`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-opt-report.md:16
msgid ""
"It provides information on the execution time, memory usage, and other "
"details of each optimization pass."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-opt-report.md:22
msgid ""
"Then, you create a report using the {program}`llvm-opt-report` command with "
"the YAML optimization record file {file}`foo.opt.yaml` as input."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-opt-report.md:28
msgid "foo.lst is the generated optimization report."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-opt-report.md:56
msgid ""
"Symbols printed on the left side of the program indicate what kind of "
"optimization was performed. The meanings of the symbols are as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-opt-report.md:59
msgid "I: The function is inlined."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-opt-report.md:60
msgid ""
"U: The loop is unrolled. The following number indicates the unroll factor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-opt-report.md:61
msgid ""
"V: The loop is vectorized. The following numbers indicate the vector length "
"and the interleave factor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-opt-report.md:64
msgid ""
"If a specific line of code is output twice, it means that the same "
"optimization pass was applied to that line of code twice, and the pass was "
"able to further optimize the code on the second iteration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-opt-report.md:68
msgid "OPTIONS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-opt-report.md:70
msgid ""
"If `input` is \"`-`\" or omitted, {program}`llvm-opt-report` reads from "
"standard input. Otherwise, it will read from the specified filename."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-opt-report.md:73
msgid ""
"If the {option}`-o` option is omitted, then {program}`llvm-opt-report` will "
"send its output to standard output. If the {option}`-o` option specifies \"`-"
"`\", then the output will also be sent to standard output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-opt-report.md:78
msgid "Display available options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-opt-report.md:82
msgid "Display the version of this program."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-opt-report.md:86
msgid ""
"The format of the optimization record file. The Argument is one of the "
"following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-opt-report.md:89
msgid "yaml"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-opt-report.md:90
msgid "bitstream"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-opt-report.md:94
msgid "Do not demangle function names."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-opt-report.md:98
msgid "Output file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-opt-report.md:102
msgid "Root for relative input paths."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-opt-report.md:106
msgid "Do not include vectorization factors, etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-opt-report.md:109
msgid "EXIT STATUS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-opt-report.md:111
msgid ""
"{program}`llvm-opt-report` returns 0 on success. Otherwise, an error message "
"is printed to standard error, and the tool returns 1."
msgstr ""
